\ ==== fill-solid ( points faces centres normals colours leads camera projection shading -- ), offline ====

\ fill-solid draws a solid's faces, an array of corner-index arrays or a
\ matrix of them a row a face, as a camera sees them: the points
\ (n×3 or n×4 rows) carried to the eye's terms by the 4×3 camera matrix,
\ each face kept when it turns toward the eye (its outward normal against
\ the eye's place less its centre), sorted farthest first by its centre's
\ depth less its lead, left out when a corner lies nearer than the near
\ plane, projected by [ focal centre-x centre-y near ], then filled and
\ outlined, each pixel kept only where the face is no farther than what
\ the same call drew there before, unless a 13th shading element is 0. A
\ face of two corners is a line: never culled, sorted by its middle, drawn
\ in its colour faded into the sky but unlit, each pixel tested against the
\ faces' depths along its length without writing its own. A face whose
\ colour has 0x1000000 set is unlit: the sun's light is left out. A face
\ of more than three corners, convex on the screen, is depth-tested as
\ triangles from its first corner, each in its own plane. Its light is the
\ sun's on it, clamped to [0, 1], over a floor of the shadow share, times
\ the day's lighting; the fill is its colour
\ dimmed to that light and faded into the sky's colour keeping a share,
\ the outline the same at the outline share of the light; grey when asked.
\ The shading is [ eye-x eye-y eye-z sun-x sun-y sun-z shadow lighting
\ kept sky outline-share grey ].

: show-rows ( bitmap -- )
	| bitmap |
	bitmap dim to n-columns to n-rows
	0 n-rows 1 do row
		"" 0 n-columns 1 do column
			bitmap row column @i,j to pixel
			pixel 0 = if "." else pixel 0x808080 = if "#" else pixel 0x404040 = if "o" else pixel 0xff0000 = if "r" else "?" then then then then +
		loop . cr
	loop ;

: blank ( -- ) 0 ink 0 0 12 12 fill-rect ;

\ the camera looks along z from the origin: a point [ x y z ] is x across, y up, z ahead
[ 1 0 0  0 1 0  0 0 1  0 0 0 ] 4 3 matrix constant straight-on
[ 10 5 5 0.1 ] vector constant projection
[ 0 0 0  0 0 -1  0.5 1 1  0  0.5 0 ] vector constant sunlit

\ a square 4 across, 10 ahead, its corners at 3 and 7 on the screen
[ -2 -2 10  2 -2 10  2 2 10  -2 2 10 ] 4 3 matrix constant square

\ === a face toward the eye: filled grey, outlined at half the light ===
blank
square [ [ 0 1 2 3 ] ] [ 0 0 10 ] 1 3 matrix [ 0 0 -1 ] 1 3 matrix [ 0x808080 ] vector [ 0 ] vector straight-on projection sunlit fill-solid
0 0 9 9 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ .........
\ .........
\ .........
\ ...ooooo.
\ ...o###o.
\ ...o###o.
\ ...o###o.
\ ...ooooo.
\ .........
clear

